Z||000009||MinnGreenGT||12-10-2001||10:39 AM||||If you had the right tools, that pontiac/flag emblem wouldn't be that difficult to create.  You'd have to create the design on the computer (simple really, especially if you scanned one of them).  Then print it out on vinyl (I have the machine to do that), then run it through a vinyl cutter, trimming the edges (Joe maybe). And finally, they make a handheld epoxy kit that creates the "bubble" on top (I don't know anyone who actually has one of these, but I had a catalog somewhere...)<P>Just a thought.<P>As to the emblem on the sides... I really like the way the nose emblem looks on the edge of the fender- I'll probably to that next time around (next paint job).<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Joe Torma||12-10-2001||11:49 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MinnGreenGT:<BR><B>If you had the right tools, that pontiac/flag emblem wouldn't be that difficult to create.  You'd have to create the design on the computer (simple really, especially if you scanned one of them).  Then print it out on vinyl (I have the machine to do that), then run it through a vinyl cutter, trimming the edges (Joe maybe). And finally, they make a handheld epoxy kit that creates the "bubble" on top (I don't know anyone who actually has one of these, but I had a catalog somewhere...)<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I've heard of that stuff too.  I can probably find a supplier for self adhesive epoxy bubble decals--I've seen them advertise somewhere.<P>I like that pontiac/flag a lot.<BR>||||reg||1
